<scenario name="The Curbside Boom" startYear="2008" startCash="16000000" difficulty="Normal" endYear="2014">
  <intro
    text="Diesel is at four dollars, the airlines are cutting regional flights, and students who would never have set foot in a bus station are booking a seat on their phones for a dollar. The new lines pick passengers up at the kerb, skip the terminal rents altogether and put double-deckers on the city pairs that pay. You have a handful of coaches and six years to build a network out of this before the boom ends." />
  <success
    text="You built a real carrier out of the curbside years, and it is making money without a terminal to its name." />
